.TH DISCOVERY.YAML 5 "2026-09-30" "mu2edaq-discovery 1.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
discovery.yaml \- configuration file for the mu2edaq-discovery tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
discovery:
  group: 239.255.42.99
  port: 28999
  timeout: 2.0
  interval: 10.0
  broadcast: [255.255.255.255]
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
A YAML file read by
.BR mu2edaq\-discover (1)
and
.BR mu2edaq\-discover\-gui (1)
when it is named by
.B \-\-config
or by
.BR MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_CONFIG .
.B There is no default path:
if neither is given, no file is read at all and the built\-in defaults apply.
The packaged copy at
.I config/discovery.yaml
is an example, not an implicitly\-loaded default.
.PP
Reading a config file requires
.BR PyYAML ,
which is otherwise not a dependency of this package.
If PyYAML is missing and
.B \-\-config
was given, the tool exits with an error rather than falling back.
.PP
Settings live under a top\-level
.B discovery:
mapping.
A file with no such key is accepted and the whole document is used as the
mapping, which is what lets a shared site config nest this section under a
larger tree.
.PP
Precedence is command line, then environment, then this file, then the
built\-in defaults.
Only the keys present are applied; anything unrecognised is ignored.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B group
Multicast group address.
Default
.BR 239.255.42.99 ,
in the administratively scoped
.B 239.0.0.0/8
range.
Changing it partitions the network: a client and a responder on different
groups cannot see each other over multicast, though the broadcast leg still
connects them.
.TP
.B port
UDP port for both queries and announcements.
Default
.BR 28999 .
Every responder in the deployment must agree.
.TP
.B timeout
Seconds a query waits for replies, as a float.
Default
.BR 2.0 .
.TP
.B interval
Auto\-probe interval in seconds for
.BR mu2edaq\-discover\-gui (1).
Default
.BR 10.0 .
Ignored by
.BR mu2edaq\-discover (1).
.TP
.B broadcast
Where to send the broadcast leg of a query, in addition to the multicast.
A YAML list of addresses, a single string, or a boolean.
.B false
(or
.BR off ", " no ", " none )
means multicast only;
.B true
(or
.BR on ", " yes ", " default )
means the limited broadcast
.BR 255.255.255.255 .
A string may also hold several addresses separated by commas or whitespace.
Default: the limited broadcast.
.PP
Responders embedded in applications do not read this file.
Their group, port and interface come from their own package's configuration
and are passed to the
.B Responder
constructor.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config/discovery.yaml
The packaged example, carrying the defaults above.
.TP
.I mu2edaq-config/config-main/mu2edaq-discovery/discovery.yaml
The deployed copy in the site configuration submodule.
It omits
.B broadcast
and, in some tagged configurations, also
.BR interval ;
the built\-in defaults then apply to those keys.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_CONFIG
Path used when
.B \-\-config
is not given.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_GROUP
.TQ
.B MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_PORT
.TQ
.B MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_TIMEOUT
.TQ
.B MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_INTERVAL
.TQ
.B MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_BROADCAST
Override the corresponding keys in this file.
.SH EXAMPLES
A multi\-homed node that must reach two DAQ subnets:
.EX
    discovery:
      port: 28999
      timeout: 3.0
      broadcast:
        - 131.225.245.255
        - 10.226.9.255
.EE
Multicast only, for diagnosing what IGMP snooping is hiding:
.EX
    discovery:
      broadcast: false
.EE
Using it:
.EX
    mu2edaq-discover --config config/discovery.yaml
    MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_CONFIG=/etc/mu2edaq/discovery.yaml mu2edaq-discover
.EE
.SH NOTES
A
.B timeout
or
.B port
of
.B 0
in this file is treated as absent, because the tools resolve each setting with
an
.B or
chain in which zero is falsy.
The built\-in default applies instead.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-discover (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-discover\-gui (1),
.BR mu2edaq_discovery (3),
.BR mu2edaq\-discovery (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ Group.
